    "interpretation": "Properly controlled test of the NON-EXACT (disformal) TEP sector via the closed synchronization loop A->sat1->B->sat2->A, i.e. the double difference. Co-located controls are null as required (WTZR-WTZZ, identical LEIAR25.R3 antennas, z=+1.1). A significant direction-dependent term survives tropospheric-gradient and antenna PCV correction, but it does NOT carry the holonomy signature: the flux must scale with enclosed loop area, and |slope| vs baseline gives Spearman -0.14 while |slope| vs the pair's own DD noise gives +0.89. The term therefore tracks site-specific systematics (multipath, which ANTEX cannot remove since it is an antenna-model average, not a site calibration), not loop geometry. NO evidence for a non-exact sector at the 10-150 mm DD-residual level; any holonomy lies below the multipath floor. THIS DOES NOT BEAR ON THE SCALAR SECTOR, which is established (Papers 1-2 distance-structured cos-phase correlation; reproduced here at 27 sigma in Step 53, and operationally exploited in the Step 64 P1 pass).",
